Read and follow the repository-root `AGENTS.md` before any work. It is the authoritative project guide and persistent record of user requirements. For frontend work, also follow `web/AGENTS.md`.

The two highest-priority repository requirements apply to every task:

- Use `docker-compose-dev.yml` for development, with mounted source and hot reload for the Vite frontend and Go backend. Start from the repository root with `docker compose -f docker-compose-dev.yml up --build -d`; preparation is documented in `docker/dev/README.md`.
- Preserve the blue-and-white UI, consistent project fonts and backgrounds, and shared component styling. Use existing semantic tokens and do not replace the primary color scheme.

Follow all remaining architecture, build, test, and validation instructions in `AGENTS.md`.
